WEBVTT


00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:03.060
Is it really possible to get a full body workout

00:00:03.061 --> 00:00:05.281
with one kettlebell in 15 minutes?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:07.440
Of course. Let me show you.

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.600
I call this complex fives.

00:00:09.740 --> 00:00:11.500
We're doing five different exercises,

00:00:11.501 --> 00:00:15.041
five reps apiece. We're gonna start with these close grip push UPS.

00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:17.440
I want you to take these slow and controlled

00:00:17.740 --> 00:00:19.440
so that we get time under tension.

00:00:19.660 --> 00:00:22.720
We can focus on the form, keeping the core tight,

00:00:22.820 --> 00:00:25.240
activating the chest and triceps.

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:29.920
We're going to take this right into the deadlift with a high pull.

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:31.640
Take your time with these reps

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:34.380
so you don't get too much momentum from the legs.

00:00:34.381 --> 00:00:36.581
So we can still get proper,

00:00:36.582 --> 00:00:39.401
proper activation of your upper body.

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:41.960
From these.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.320
We'll go straight into five kettlebell swings.

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.440
As always focusing on the hip hinge,

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:52.440
finding that tension through the glutes and the hamstrings.

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.560
We're gonna take this right into five goblet squats,

00:00:58.180 --> 00:01:01.920
dropping down below 90 degrees and driving the ground away from you.

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.800
And last but not least, we got five push press.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:15.620
Repeat that complex as many times as you can in 15 minutes,

00:01:15.621 --> 00:01:18.461
and you got yourself a perfectly adequate full body workout.

00:01:18.462 --> 00:01:22.121
If you like efficient and effective workouts using minimal equipment,

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:24.160
give me a follow. We'll see you next time.
